    (t1 = kap + 2(P-k+)k- - i0 has its k- pole at -kap/2(P-k+) + i0; t2 = kap + 2P'k+ - 2k+k- - i0 has its k+ pole
     at -kap/2(P'-k-) + i0: both lie in the upper half planes, so the Glauber region is left by Im k+- < 0.)
   h1Y = 2P(k- - e k+) - i0                  : Im(factor)/d =   -1.41071, prescription sign -1 -> compatible
   h2Y = 2P'(k+ - e k-) - i0  [sigma=+1]     : Im(factor)/d =   -1.41071, prescription sign -1 -> compatible
   h2Y = 2P'(k+ - e k-) + i0  [sigma=-1]     : Im(factor)/d =   -1.41071, prescription sign +1 -> OBSTRUCTS the deformation
